BT 1 0 0 1 0 108.75 Tm 13.25 TL /F2 10.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (We release eight historical-data repair contracts across six Python projects, with 65 historical files and 252) Tj T* (dependent observations of reading, continued use and persistence. The resource makes acceptance explicit when) Tj T* (old formats lose information. Two repairs satisfy an 84-observation numeric contract, although literal reference) Tj T* (equality rejects 60 observations for one valid repair. A separate calibration of a known AI SDK defect tests the) Tj T* -0.06175 Tw (opposite boundary: rejecting ambiguous authorization while preserving safe legacy approvals. The original Gemma) Tj T* 0 Tw (baseline accepts four of 32 repairs. A new, single-deployment comparison completes 64 attempts: exact-text) Tj T* (editing accepts 10/32, versus 4/32 for a version-checked line-span interface. All complete-acceptance decisions) Tj T* -0.048429 Tw (survive API-free replay. Historical bytes, source patches, negative results and API-free verifiers are released. Code,) Tj T* 0 Tw (data and paper: ) Tj .117647 .270588 .341176 rg (https://github.com/GuilinDev/historical-data-repair-contracts/releases/tag/v0.1.2) Tj T* ET
